# Conventional Commits (English only)

Use English Conventional Commits:

```
<type>(optional-scope): <short summary>
```

- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `test`, `docs`, `chore`, `ci`, `build`, `perf`, `style`, `revert`.
- Imperative summary, lowercase after type, no trailing period, about 72 chars.
- Optional body explains why, not a file list.
- Use a scope (`web`, `api`, `i18n`, `docker`, `agent`) only when useful.
- Avoid vague summaries and unrelated changes in one commit.
